  "$contactComment": "Omnio is a demonstration marketplace, not a trading entity. These are placeholders reserved for exactly this purpose: the address uses the .example TLD that RFC 2606 reserves for documentation, the number is in Ofcom's reserved drama range (+44 20 7946 0xxx) and can never reach a real person, and EC1A 1BB is Royal Mail's own documented example postcode. Nothing here is a fabricated credential presented as genuine, which is why registration stays null rather than carrying an invented company number. A real deployment replaces every value and sets isDemonstration to false.",
  "contact": {
    "isDemonstration": true,
    "entity": "Omnio",
    "email": "hello@omnio.example",
    "phone": "+44 20 7946 0142",
    "address": "1 Example Street, London EC1A 1BB, United Kingdom",
    "hours": "Monday to Friday, 09:00-17:00 GMT",
    "responseTime": "within one working day",
    "registration": null
  },
  "crossSell": {
    "$comment": "Selldone's cross-sell is a backoffice feature and XAPI does not expose it to the storefront, so the pairing lives here. `pairs` names companions for specific products; anything not listed falls back to the best-ranked promotion-safe products from the same department. Prices shown are always the live catalog prices — no bundle discount is invented, because a discount this storefront cannot apply at checkout would be a false claim.",
    "maxItems": 2,
    "fallback": "same-department",
